FINDINGS #C968 9977c28 (Security 11-11), diffed against its parent 65575d2.
F1 (must fix): Workers Builds installs dependencies automatically before the build command (Cloudflare's build-image page; skippable with the build variable SKIP_DEPENDENCY_INSTALL=1). A preinstall or prepare script added to package.json on main would then run BEFORE the hash-pinned gate, inside the build, possibly with the token in its environment, and could plant a fake sha256sum, node or git on PATH so the gate passes. Fix: docs/self-deploy.md step 3 sets SKIP_DEPENDENCY_INSTALL=1 (the deploy needs no npm dependencies; npx fetches the pinned wrangler), and the gate refuses unless that variable is 1 or true.
F2 (must fix): the gate reads notes on the tip only. Main can be pushed directly (no GitHub enforcement on a free private repo), so an unreviewed commit under a signed tip would deploy. Mirror the release tool: every commit in <current BUILD_SHA>..<commit> carries SECURE (and PASS as the release tool requires).
LOW1: if the build's clone is shallow (docs silent), merge-base fails and every build refuses (fail closed, but dead): fetch enough history (git fetch --unshallow, or deepen to the BUILD_SHA) before the ancestor check.
Still reaches (one-account trade-off, #T1837): the custom token (Workers Scripts Edit, D1 Edit, Account Settings Read) can replace or delete any Worker on the account, including the product's production Worker and flight-board-state, and read or change every D1 database; not DNS, routes, Access, zones or R2. Checked and fine: custom user token, never the auto-created one; no routes in wrangler.board.toml and none passed (as the pair); the gate is first in the build command and hash-pinned by the owner; nothing on the Mac or in GitHub Actions; deploy command set to a no-op; redact covers token, account and config; the phone push fires once per BUILD_SHA.
